{"id":"mahabharata-9-058","work":"mahabharata","part":9,"partName":"शल्यपर्व","partNameEn":"Shalya Parva","unit":58,"title":"अष्टपञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 58 · Bhima breaks Duryodhana's thigh","summary":{"en":"Bhima strikes Duryodhana's thighs with his mace and he falls like a great sal-tree, and Bhima kicks his head. Yudhishthira rebukes him, and Bhima says he has fulfilled his vow, and Duryodhana laments his unjust fall.","kn":"ಭೀಮ ಗದೆಯಿಂದ ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನ ತೊಡೆಗಳಿಗೆ ಹೊಡೆಯಲು ಅವನು ಮಹಾ ಸಾಲವೃಕ್ಷದಂತೆ ಉರುಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಭೀಮ ಅವನ ತಲೆಗೆ ಒದೆಯುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಖಂಡಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಪ್ರತಿಜ್ಞೆ ಪೂರೈಸಿದೆನೆಂದು ಭೀಮ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ದುರ್ಯೋಧನ ಅನ್ಯಾಯದ ಪತನಕ್ಕೆ ವಿಲಪಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"भीम गदा से दुर्योधन की जंघाओं पर प्रहार करते हैं और वह विशाल साल वृक्ष की तरह गिरता है, और भीम उसके सिर पर लात मारते हैं। युधिष्ठिर उन्हें फटकारते हैं, भीम कहते हैं कि प्रतिज्ञा पूरी हुई, और दुर्योधन अपने अन्यायपूर्ण पतन पर विलाप करता है।","te":"భీముడు గదతో దుర్యోధనుని తొడలను కొట్టగా అతడు మహా సాల వృక్షంలా కూలుతాడు; భీముడు అతని తలను తన్నుతాడు. యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అతన్ని గద్దిస్తాడు; ప్రతిజ్ఞ నెరవేరిందని భీముడు చెబుతాడు; దుర్యోధనుడు తన అన్యాయ పతనానికి విలపిస్తాడు.","ta":"பீமன் கதையால் துரியோதனனின் தொடைகளைத் தாக்க, அவன் பெரிய சாலமரம் போல் வீழ்கிறான்; பீமன் அவன் தலையை உதைக்கிறான். யுதிஷ்டிரர் கடிய, சபதம் நிறைவேறியது என்று பீமன் கூற, துரியோதனன் தன் அநியாய வீழ்ச்சிக்குப் புலம்புகிறான்.","ml":"ഭീമൻ ഗദകൊണ്ട് ദുര്യോധനന്റെ തുടകളിൽ അടിക്കുന്നു; വലിയ സാൽ വൃക്ഷംപോലെ അദ്ദേഹം വീഴുന്നു, ഭീമൻ തലയിൽ ചവിട്ടുന്നു. യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ഭീമനെ ശാസിക്കുന്നു; പ്രതിജ്ഞ നിറവേറ്റിയെന്ന് ഭീമൻ പറയുന്നു; അന്യായമായി വീഴ്ത്തപ്പെട്ടതിൽ ദുര്യോധനൻ വിലപിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 9.58; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jun 23 2020","sections":[{"title":"गदायुद्धपर्व","titleEn":"Gadayuddha Parva (The mace fight)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तं पातितं ततो दृष्ट्वा महाशालमिवोद्गतम् ।\nप्रहृष्टमनसः सर्वे बभूवुस्तत्र पाण्डवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him fallen like a great sala tree torn up, all the Pandavas there were glad at heart."}},{"n":2,"text":"उन्मत्तमिव मातङ्गं सिंहेन विनिपातितम् ।\nददृशुर्हृष्टरोमाणः सर्वे ते चापि सोमकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Somakas too all saw him, hair bristling with joy, like a maddened elephant brought down by a lion."}},{"n":3,"text":"ततो दुर्योधनं हत्वा भीमसेनः प्रतापवान् ।\nपतितं कौरवेन्द्रं तमुपगम्येदमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then mighty Bhimasena, having struck Duryodhana down, went up to the fallen king of the Kurus and said this."}},{"n":4,"text":"गौर्गौरिति पुरा मन्द द्रौपदीमेकवाससम् ।\nयत्सभायां हसन्नस्मांस्तदा वदसि दुर्मते ।\nतस्यावहासस्य फलमद्य त्वं समवाप्नुहि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Fool, you once laughed at us in the assembly and called Draupadi, in her single garment, 'cow, cow'; reap today the fruit of that mockery, evil-minded man.\""}},{"n":5,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा स वामेन पदा मौलिमुपास्पृशत् ।\nशिरश्च राजसिंहस्य पादेन समलोडयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, he touched the king's head with his left foot, and with his foot he rolled the lion among kings by the head."}},{"n":6,"text":"तथैव क्रोधसंरक्तो भीमः परबलार्दनः ।\nपुनरेवाब्रवीद्वाक्यं यत्तच्छृणु नराधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhima, scorcher of enemy armies, his eyes red with anger, spoke again; hear his words, lord of men."}},{"n":7,"text":"येऽस्मान्पुरोऽपनृत्यन्त पुनर्गौरिति गौरिति ।\nतान्वयं प्रतिनृत्यामः पुनर्गौरिति गौरिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Those who danced before us, crying 'cow, cow' again and again, we now dance back at, crying 'cow, cow' again and again.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"नास्माकं निकृतिर्वह्निर्नाक्षद्यूतं न वञ्चना ।\nस्वबाहुबलमाश्रित्य प्रबाधामो वयं रिपून् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"We have no cheating, no fire-setting, no dice play, no fraud; we crush our enemies relying on the strength of our own arms.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"सोऽवाप्य वैरस्य परस्य पारं\nवृकोदरः प्राह शनैः प्रहस्य ।\nयुधिष्ठिरं केशवसृञ्जयांश्च\nधनंजयं माद्रवतीसुतौ च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having reached the far shore of that great enmity, Vrikodara said softly, with a laugh, to Yudhishthira, Keshava, the Srinjayas, Dhananjaya and the two sons of Madri:"}},{"n":10,"text":"रजस्वलां द्रौपदीमानयन्ये\nये चाप्यकुर्वन्त सदस्यवस्त्राम् ।\nतान्पश्यध्वं पाण्डवैर्धार्तराष्ट्रा-\nन्रणे हतांस्तपसा याज्ञसेन्याः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Look at those who dragged Draupadi in her monthly course into the assembly and who pulled at her clothes in the hall: these sons of Dhritarashtra, killed in battle by the Pandavas, through the austerity of Yajnasena's daughter.\""}},{"n":11,"text":"ये नः पुरा षण्ढतिलानवोच-\nन्क्रूरा राज्ञो धृतराष्ट्रस्य पुत्राः ।\nते नो हताः सगणाः सानुबन्धाः\nकामं स्वर्गं नरकं वा व्रजामः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The cruel sons of King Dhritarashtra who long ago called us 'barren sesame', impotent men, have been killed with their followers and kinsmen; now let us go to heaven or hell as we please.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"पुनश्च राज्ञः पतितस्य भूमौ\nस तां गदां स्कन्धगतां निरीक्ष्य ।\nवामेन पादेन शिरः प्रमृद्य\nदुर्योधनं नैकृतिकेत्यवोचत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Again, looking at that mace on the shoulder of the king fallen on the ground, he pressed down Duryodhana's head with his left foot and called him a cheat."}},{"n":13,"text":"हृष्टेन राजन्कुरुपार्थिवस्य\nक्षुद्रात्मना भीमसेनेन पादम् ।\nदृष्ट्वा कृतं मूर्धनि नाभ्यनन्द-\nन्धर्मात्मानः सोमकानां प्रबर्हाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"O king, the righteous leaders of the Somakas did not approve on seeing that Bhimasena, petty and gleeful, had put his foot on the Kuru king's head."}},{"n":14,"text":"तव पुत्रं तथा हत्वा कत्थमानं वृकोदरम् ।\nनृत्यमानं च बहुशो धर्मराजोऽब्रवीदिदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Bhima had struck down your son, and went on boasting and dancing again and again, King Yudhishthira said this."}},{"n":15,"text":"मा शिरोऽस्य पदा मर्दीर्मा धर्मस्तेऽत्यगान्महान् ।\nराजा ज्ञातिर्हतश्चायं नैतन्न्याय्यं तवानघ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Do not trample his head with your foot; do not let your great dharma be violated. He is a king and a kinsman, and he has been struck down; this is not right for you, blameless one.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"विध्वस्तोऽयं हतामात्यो हतभ्राता हतप्रजः ।\nउत्सन्नपिण्डो भ्राता च नैतन्न्याय्यं कृतं त्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He is ruined, his ministers, brothers and sons are killed, and the line of offerings to his ancestors is cut off; Bhima, you did not act rightly.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"धार्मिको भीमसेनोऽसावित्याहुस्त्वां पुरा जनाः ।\nस कस्माद्भीमसेन त्वं राजानमधितिष्ठसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"People once called you the righteous Bhimasena; why, then, do you stand on the king, Bhimasena?\""}},{"n":18,"text":"दृष्ट्वा दुर्योधनं राजा कुन्तीपुत्रस्तथागतम् ।\nनेत्राभ्यामश्रुपूर्णाभ्यामिदं वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Duryodhana in that state, King Yudhishthira, son of Kunti, his eyes full of tears, said this."}},{"n":19,"text":"नूनमेतद्बलवता धात्रादिष्टं महात्मना ।\nयद्वयं त्वां जिघांसामस्त्वं चास्मान्कुरुसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Surely this was ordained by the mighty and great Creator: that we would wish to kill you, best of Kurus, and you us.\""}},{"n":20,"text":"आत्मनो ह्यपराधेन महद्व्यसनमीदृशम् ।\nप्राप्तवानसि यल्लोभान्मदाद्बाल्याच्च भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"By your own fault you have fallen into such great misfortune, Bharata, through greed, pride and childishness.\""}},{"n":21,"text":"घातयित्वा वयस्यांश्च भ्रातॄनथ पितॄंस्तथा ।\nपुत्रान्पौत्रांस्तथाचार्यांस्ततोऽसि निधनं गतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Having had friends, brothers, fathers, sons, grandsons and teachers killed, you have now met your own end.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"तवापराधादस्माभिर्भ्रातरस्ते महारथाः ।\nनिहता ज्ञातयश्चान्ये दिष्टं मन्ये दुरत्ययम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Because of your fault our brothers, great chariot-warriors, and other kinsmen were killed by us; I think fate is hard to cross.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"स्नुषाश्च प्रस्नुषाश्चैव धृतराष्ट्रस्य विह्वलाः ।\nगर्हयिष्यन्ति नो नूनं विधवाः शोककर्शिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Dhritarashtra's daughters-in-law and granddaughters-in-law, widowed, distraught and wasted by grief, will surely blame us.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा सुदुःखार्तो निशश्वास स पार्थिवः ।\nविललाप चिरं चापि धर्मपुत्रो युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, in deep grief the king sighed, and Yudhishthira, son of Dharma, wept for a long time."}}]}]}